<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Norse–Gaels</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gall-Ghàidheil, Gall-Gaedil, Norse-Gaels, Gallgaels, Gall-Gaidheil</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Norse–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaels">Gaels</a> were people of mixed Scandinavian and Gaelic descent and culture who emerged in Ireland, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrides">Hebrides</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> from the 9th century. They dominated the Kingdom of the Isles and the Isle of Man, and their Gaelic name, Gall-Ghàidheil, survives in Galloway. Rulers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/godred-crovan">Godred Crovan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somerled">Somerled</a> came from this world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/norse-gaels.jpg" alt="Norse–Gaels" width="320" height="336" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sémhur · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_Mann_and_the_Isles-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
